    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Change\n\nConsolidated the three separate owner duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived **`identityKey`** = `normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + (householdId or empty)`. A create is now rejected with **409 only when the new owner's whole `identityKey` equals an existing owner's**.\n\nBecause the telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with different telephones now produce different keys and are both allowed \u2014 only an exact full-key match is a duplicate.\n\n## What changed\n\n**New:**\n- `OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 shared helper deriving the key (`key(...)`), plus E.164/email normalization and the deterministic `householdId(...)`, so the key computed at the check, the id assigned to the entity, and the key returned in the response are all computed identically.\n- `EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 the single check function. The new owner's household component is the id it *will* be assigned (deterministic when `sharesHousehold: true`, otherwise empty), matching `AssignOwnerHousehold`.\n- `DuplicateIdentityException` + handler + `officefloor/escalation/...DuplicateIdentityException.yml` (409).\n\n**Edited:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 the three `ensureUnique*` steps replaced by one `ensureUniqueIdentity`.\n- `AssignOwnerHousehold.java` \u2014 now derives the household id via `OwnerIdentity.householdId(...)` (removed the duplicated SHA-256 logic) so it can't drift from the check.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the read-only `identityKey` field to the `Owner` schema.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 maps `identityKey` from the owner's telephone/email/householdId, so it's **returned** in the response.\n\n**Removed** (obsolete): `EnsureUniqueOwnerEmail/Telephone/Household`, the `DuplicateEmail/Telephone/Household` exceptions + handlers, and their escalation YAMLs.\n\nVerification: `./mvnw -o test` \u2192 `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (the `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsIdentityCollision` case, which asserts a same-telephone create returns 409), `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
